{
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "notes": [
    "Skill ontology used by app/core/skills.py.",
    "",
    "SHAPE",
    "  Each entry is {name, category, aliases}. `name` is the canonical form",
    "  shown in the UI. `aliases` are extra surface forms that map to it.",
    "  Matching is case-insensitive; you do NOT need to list case variants.",
    "",
    "  Multi-word names are matched as whole phrases, so 'machine learning'",
    "  will not fire on a document that only contains the word 'learning'.",
    "",
    "CATEGORIES",
    "  language | framework | database | cloud | devops | data | ml |",
    "  tool | practice | soft",
    "",
    "  Categories drive the grouped display on the report screen and the",
    "  cohort heatmap. Keep the set small; a long tail of one-off categories",
    "  makes the UI unreadable.",
    "",
    "EXPANDING THIS FILE",
    "  This ships with a curated technology list. To grow it to full coverage,",
    "  download the ESCO skills taxonomy (free, ec.europa.eu/esco) and merge",
    "  the 'skill' concepts in with category 'practice'. Run",
    "  scripts/validate_skills.py afterwards - not yet written; when it exists it",
    "  aliases that collide across entries, which silently break matching."
  ],

